# React Native components and lists

## Components

- Reuse the project's UI primitives (buttons, fields, cards, dialogs, toasts) before creating new ones; never `Alert.alert` when the app has its own dialog.
- `Pressable` for touchables, with a hit area of at least 44×44 (`hitSlop` on small icons) and visible press feedback (`android_ripple` on Android, opacity on iOS).
- Every icon-only control has `accessibilityRole` and `accessibilityLabel` in the UI language.
- Text only inside `<Text>`; bound font scaling (`maxFontSizeMultiplier`) only on tight badges and tab labels, not body text.
- Colors come from the theme hook so dark mode and themes apply; no static color imports in components that render themed surfaces.

## Safe areas

- `SafeAreaView` / `useSafeAreaInsets` from `react-native-safe-area-context`, never from `react-native`. Android is edge-to-edge: pad content and bottom bars with insets.

## Lists

- `FlatList` (or `FlashList` if the project already has it) for any unbounded data; give it `style={{ flex: 1 }}` or a bounded parent.
- Stable `keyExtractor` from the record id, never the index.
- Never put a vertical virtualized list inside a vertical `ScrollView`; use `ListHeaderComponent` / `ListFooterComponent`.
- Memoize `renderItem` and row components when rows are non-trivial; page or window large data instead of loading everything.

## Visuals and motion

- Shadows: RN 0.76+ `boxShadow` works on both platforms; with legacy `shadow*` props add `elevation` on Android, and never give an elevated view a transparent background.
- Images: use what the project has (`expo-image` only if installed); always set explicit size and `resizeMode` / `contentFit`.
- Animations with Reanimated shared values; animate `transform` and `opacity`, use layout animations for size changes.
